{"title":"Career roadmap · Behavioural Analyst","role":"Behavioural Analyst","summary":"A Behavioural Analyst studies how people behave, what influences behaviour, how behaviour changes across contexts, and how interventions can improve outcomes. Depending on the setting, the role can involve behavioural research, consumer behaviour, organisational behaviour, education, behavioural science, UX research, public policy or applied behaviour analysis.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starting point"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"BA Psychology / BA Psychology Honours"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"Behavioural Analyst"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Humanities & Social Sciences → Psychology → Behavioural Science"}],[{"text":"Core disciplines"},{"text":"Psychology, behavioural science, research methods, statistics"}],[{"text":"Technical stack"},{"text":"Excel, SPSS/R/Python, survey tools, data visualisation"}],[{"text":"Research stack"},{"text":"Experimental design, observation, surveys, interviews, behavioural measurement"}],[{"text":"Strong PG routes"},{"text":"MA/M.Sc Psychology, Behavioural Science, Cognitive Science, Organisational Psychology, Applied Psychology"}],[{"text":"Important distinction"},{"text":"Clinical/applied practice may require additional qualifications"}],[{"text":"Long-term direction"},{"text":"Behavioural Analyst → Behavioural Scientist/Specialist → Lead/Research/Strategy"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Research, behavioural science, UX, consumer insights and HR internships"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Psychology/behavioural science PG + analyst role"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Behavioural Analyst / Behavioural Scientist"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Behavioural strategy, experimentation, AI-human behaviour research and leadership"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A BA Psychology provides an excellent foundation, but “Behavioural Analyst” is a broad career title rather than one universally regulated profession. Students should distinguish between behavioural-science/consumer/organisational roles and clinical or applied behaviour-analysis roles that may require additional specialised qualifications, supervised practice or local professional requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Psychology","Behavioural Research/UX/Consumer/Organisational Internship","Research/Behavioural Associate","Behavioural Analyst","Senior Behavioural Analyst","Behavioural Scientist / Behavioural Strategy Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"For a student specifically targeting Applied Behaviour Analysis (ABA), the pathway should be treated separately and planned around the qualification and supervised-practice requirements of the country and employer."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"University + open academic resources"},{"text":"Psychology concept portfolio"},{"text":"Foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Observation + behavioural recording"},{"text":"Research-methods coursework"},{"text":"Behaviour observation study"},{"text":"Measurement"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Statistics + research methods"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Quantitative skills"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Experimental psychology"},{"text":"University/lab work"},{"text":"Small experiment"},{"text":"Research"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Behavioural data analysis"},{"text":"Excel/R/Python/SPSS"},{"text":"Behavioural dataset analysis"},{"text":"Analytics"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Behavioural internship"},{"text":"Research/UX/consumer/HR organisation"},{"text":"Internship + project"},{"text":"Professional skills"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Advanced coursework"},{"text":"Specialised research project"},{"text":"Career direction"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"PG/recruitment preparation"},{"text":"University + employer requirements"},{"text":"Research portfolio"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For a 3-year BA, compress the Year 4 activities into the final year."},{"type":"h","text":"Core knowledge stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Psychology"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong foundations in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Social psychology"},{"text":"Developmental psychology"},{"text":"Personality"},{"text":"Learning and conditioning"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Emotion"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Perception"},{"text":"Psychological assessment"},{"text":"Individual differences"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is to understand why behaviour occurs, not simply describe what people do."}]},{"heading":"Behavioural science","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Behavioural economics"},{"text":"Decision science"},{"text":"Cognitive biases"},{"text":"Heuristics"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Habit formation"},{"text":"Choice architecture"},{"text":"Nudging"},{"text":"Social influence"},{"text":"Persuasion"},{"text":"Behaviour change"},{"text":"Risk perception"},{"text":"Consumer decision-making"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important concepts include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Loss aversion"},{"text":"Anchoring"},{"text":"Availability"},{"text":"Confirmation bias"},{"text":"Status quo bias"},{"text":"Framing"},{"text":"Present bias"},{"text":"Social proof"},{"text":"Reciprocity"},{"text":"Default effects"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to distinguish evidence-supported behavioural effects from oversimplified internet versions of behavioural psychology."}]},{"heading":"Research methodology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Behavioural Analyst needs strong research skills."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research questions"},{"text":"Hypotheses"},{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Operational definitions"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Control groups"},{"text":"Randomisation"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Longitudinal studies"},{"text":"Cross-sectional studies"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Mixed methods"},{"text":"Reliability"},{"text":"Validity"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Reproducibility"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong analyst should be able to answer:"},{"type":"p","text":"How do we know that the observed behavioural change was actually caused by the intervention?"}]},{"heading":"Statistics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"h","text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Mode"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Percentiles"},{"text":"Distributions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Inferential statistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"t-tests"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Chi-square"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Regression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced foundation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Experimental statistics"},{"text":"Effect sizes"},{"text":"Statistical power"},{"text":"A/B testing"},{"text":"Mediation/moderation concepts"},{"text":"Causal inference"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Remember:"},{"type":"p","text":"Correlation does not establish causation."}]},{"heading":"Behavioural measurement","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to measure:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frequency"},{"text":"Duration"},{"text":"Latency"},{"text":"Intensity"},{"text":"Response rate"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Choice"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Task completion"},{"text":"Adherence"},{"text":"Satisfaction"},{"text":"Behaviour change"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For applied settings, understand the difference between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Observable behaviour","Measurement","Intervention","Outcome"]}]},{"heading":"Data and technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pivot Tables"},{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"SUMIFS"},{"text":"IF"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Statistical calculations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistical tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with one or more:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SPSS"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Jamovi"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful libraries:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"matplotlib"},{"text":"scipy"},{"text":"statsmodels"},{"text":"scikit-learn"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Visualisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Behavioural dashboards"},{"text":"Cohort analysis"},{"text":"Funnel analysis"},{"text":"Experimental results"},{"text":"Distribution plots"},{"text":"Effect-size visualisation"}]}]},{"heading":"Qualitative research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Behaviour cannot always be understood from numbers alone."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Semi-structured interviews"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Coding"},{"text":"Participant diaries"},{"text":"Journey mapping"},{"text":"Ethnographic methods"},{"text":"Contextual inquiry"}]},{"type":"p","